                "reply_count": 6,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "The Budget I helped pass last week makes major investments in our Veterans:\n\n+ $2.3B for VA medical care\n+ $22B for the Toxic Exposures Fund \u2014 fully funding PACT Act implementation\n+ $2.2B for mental health, including $698M for suicide prevention and $313M for the Veterans Crisis Line\n+ $96M for women Veterans\u2019 healthcare\n$275M for construction grants \u2014 great news for the Long Island State Veterans Home\n$150M for cemetery grants \u2014 supporting Calverton National Cemetery\n\nAs a Navy Veteran who deployed overseas three times, I\u2019ll always fight to ensure our Veterans get the care, benefits, and respect they earned. This budget is a major step forward for Long Island and for our nation\u2019s Veterans.",
                "text_lang": "en",
