                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 13,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Health care still isn\u2019t affordable under the so-called ACA. Since it passed without a single R vote, premiums are up 60% faster than inflation, 1 in 3 claims is denied, and insurers are making record profits while families get squeezed.\nI\u2019m working with a bipartisan group on a fix to: protect LI families from premium spikes, fix Medicaid drug-pricing rules, extend open enrollment, add fraud guardrails, and force bipartisan affordability reforms by July 2026.\nReal relief that puts patients \u2014 not insurers \u2014 first.",
                "text_lang": "en",
